@startuml state-appointment
!include _style.iuml
title Appointment lifecycle (enforced in domain/Lifecycle.scala)
hide empty description
state NO_SHOW <<off>>
skinparam state<<off>> {
  BackgroundColor #EEF0F0
  BorderColor #A7B0B4
  FontColor #7D878C
}

[*] --> HELD : customer picks a time\n(POST /api/appointments/holds)
[*] --> CONFIRMED : customer books directly\n(POST /api/appointments)
HELD --> CONFIRMED : customer confirms before\nhold_expires_at (POST …/confirm)
HELD --> CANCELLED : customer releases the hold
HELD --> EXPIRED : hold ran out (system: booking flow,\njob move, confirm, or HoldSweeper)
CONFIRMED --> IN_PROGRESS : the assigned technician starts\n(any time, also before the booked start)\n<color:#7D878C>advisor / admin: not in this version</color>
IN_PROGRESS --> AWAITING_PAYMENT : the assigned technician finishes\n(the customer has checked the vehicle)\n<color:#7D878C>advisor / admin: not in this version</color>
AWAITING_PAYMENT --> COMPLETED : the assigned technician\nrecords the payment\n<color:#7D878C>admin: not in this version</color>
CONFIRMED --> CANCELLED : customer before the start time\n<color:#7D878C>advisor / admin before work starts:</color>\n<color:#7D878C>not in this version</color>
CONFIRMED -[#B5BFBB]-> NO_SHOW : <color:#7D878C>advisor / admin, after the start time</color>\n<color:#7D878C>(not in this version)</color>
CONFIRMED -[#B5BFBB]-> CONFIRMED : <color:#7D878C>workshop controller / admin moves</color>\n<color:#7D878C>the job (not in this version)</color>
COMPLETED --> [*]
CANCELLED --> [*]
NO_SHOW -[#B5BFBB]-> [*]
EXPIRED --> [*]

note right of HELD
  A hold lasts 10 minutes (HOLD_MINUTES).
  HELD, CONFIRMED and IN_PROGRESS take the bay,
  the technician and the vehicle: the database's
  EXCLUDE constraints apply to these three (V2).
end note

note right of AWAITING_PAYMENT
  The work is done: the bay, technician and
  vehicle are free again (V3). The technician
  closes the job once the customer has paid.
end note
legend bottom right
  Grey: not in this version of the web app (the backend still has it)
endlegend
@enduml
